WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.979
JAMIE: What does "climbed too far"
actually mean, though?

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:03.959
JAMIE: That phrase gets used every
time anything goes

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:05.938
JAMIE: up.

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:09.042
RUFUS: Fair. What it means in
practice is that

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.037
RUFUS: enough investors decided
the previous day's gain wasn't

00:00:12.037 --> 00:00:15.031
RUFUS: supported by new evidence
of actual value —

00:00:15.031 --> 00:00:18.026
RUFUS: earnings, products,
contracts — and started selling.
Yesterday's

00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:21.020
RUFUS: price move was the belief.
Today's reversal was

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.015
RUFUS: the doubt. That's what AP
is describing.

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.594
JAMIE: Okay, but here's what I
keep coming back

00:00:26.594 --> 00:00:29.063
JAMIE: to. When the Nasdaq drops
1.5% because "AI

00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:31.532
JAMIE: stocks reversed," people
with index funds just had

00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:34.002
JAMIE: a bad day and they probably
don't know

00:00:34.002 --> 00:00:36.471
JAMIE: why. They didn't make a bet
on AI

00:00:36.471 --> 00:00:38.940
JAMIE: valuations.
